## Why This Is Asked

This question tests triage of a mixed HTTP, MongoDB, Vault path and teaches safe caching of per-request secrets, a common beginner pitfall.

## Key Concepts

- Latency breakdown and instrumentation
- Vault per-request secret calls vs caching
- MongoDB indexing and query patterns
- Safe TTL-based cache and rotation

## Code Example

```javascript
class VaultCache {
  constructor(fetchFn, ttlMs = 60000) {
    this.fetchFn = fetchFn;
    this.ttl = ttlMs;
    this.cache = new Map();
  }
  async get(key) {
    const now = Date.now();
    const cached = this.cache.get(key);
    if (cached && now - cached.ts < this.ttl) return cached.value;
    const value = await this.fetchFn(key);
    this.cache.set(key, { value, ts: now });
    return value;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test cache invalidation after Vault rotation?
- What metrics would you monitor to ensure no stale secrets are used during load?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests cross-service atomicity and failure handling across CNPA components.

## Key Concepts
- Transactional outbox pattern
- Exactly-once semantics with Kafka transactions
- Idempotent Snowflake ingestion via dedupe keys
- End-to-end verification and monitoring

## Code Example
```sql
CREATE TABLE outbox (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY,
  aggregate_id UUID,
  payload JSONB,
  emitted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
  emitted_at TIMESTAMPTZ
);
```

```sql
BEGIN;
UPDATE users SET name='...' WHERE id=...;
INSERT INTO outbox (id, aggregate_id, payload) VALUES (gen_random_uuid(), ?, to_jsonb(...));
COMMIT;
```

```javascript
// worker pseudo
while (row = nextOutbox()) {
  kafkaProducer.send({topic:'users', value: row.payload, transaction: true});
  markEmitted(row.id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What failure modes would you test (Kafka publish fail after DB commit; DB crash during txn; consumer offset commit failure)?
- How would you scale the solution to high cardinality events and ensure end-to-end latency remains within SLOs?
